# fixedbugs, defect 555, lane b18-ffi, 2026-10-10 (panel 202's C1; the
# critic's `clash`).
#
# This module binds `twice` from a header declaring it of `double`, and
# another binds it from one declaring it of `long long`; a third module's
# header defines it. Each module's unit compiles its own header alone, and
# the linker joins the two declarations to one symbol, so C called the
# `long long` function through a `double` prototype: until 2026-10-10 this
# built at exit 0 and printed `4.0` for `twice(x: 4.0)`. Both
# declarations are told now, with clang's canonical types, before anything
# links.
use fixedbugs555/long_twice
use fixedbugs555/defines

extern "fixedbugs-555-double.h"
    function twice(x: f64) -> f64  #~ ffi_declared_two_ways

function main()
    print(long_twice.doubled(x: 3))
    print(twice(x: 4.0))
    print(defines.unit())
